ven or Ricketts ahead by a few points. Ricketts holds a large fundraising edge and benefits from incumbency, while Osborn has raised a surprisingly strong $5.7 million with minimal outside help.\n\nThe race tightened in September amid negative advertising, a leaked-audio controversy involving Osborn, and a planned Trump visit to campaign for Ricketts. Most expert raters call the race Likely R, with a couple at Lean R, and prediction markets price Ricketts around 70-75%. The forecast expects Ricketts to win by a modest margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin and sponsor-skewed polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -4.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1701, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.215, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2151, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1705, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.217, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2062, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2084, "margin": -5.0}]}